> I had a similar problem just today.  What I ended up doing is dropping
> all my stuff except my wielded weapon, then walking through the rock,
> and beating the enemy behind it (It was only a Leprachaun).
> 
> I'm no expert in Nethack, but it seemed to work...  is this the best
> thing to do?

Depends on *what* is behind the boulder-- I wouldn't like to face a troll,
or even a human zombie, bare-handed. Can you detect monsters, or do you
have telepathy?

I usually zap it with non-destructive wands or spells (magic missile,
lightning, fire, cold, drain life; not force bolt or a wand of striking,
which break boulders) or, failing that, throw things at it. Daggers and
darts are good, but you can use rocks (just don't break a Sokoban boulder
to get them, go all the way down and break a boulder or a statue on the
level with the two staircases or the Oracle level). Note that while you
can't pass the boulder, and the monster can't, spells (except force
bolts) and objects just fly past it.

If you can't kill whatever's behind the boulder, you can break the boulder
to get at it (luck penalty) or teleport boulder and monster away (no luck
penalty, but on this level at this stage the boulder is bound to end up
in an awkward place). Or go away and come back later when you do have the
means to deal with it.

   Raisse, killed by a boulder

